At first you think it's your parents came to help, but then, you obviously discern half-naked bodies, wriggling in some wild dance. No, those are certainly not parents, but savages, dwellers of the Wild Island!
Your first inducement is to run away from here as fast as possible! Then you calm down, and curiosity takes over. You don't know where to run anyway, the savages apparently can't see you. Perhaps by observing them, you'll find out how to get out of here.
You carefully tiptoe your way through rustling tangles of reed to the opposite shore. Yes, exactly so, these are natives, hosts of the Wild Island. They're dressed in loincloths, holding stone spears and clubs in their hands. Savages dance around a high pole with a totem, which meaning is hidden from you.